  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Impunity Watch (IW) - Resisting Impunity, Centring Victims: Building Ecosystems for Meaningful Transitional Justice</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Impunity Watch&#x2019;s 2026&#x2013;2031 programme aims to strengthen transitional justice, accountability and the rule of law in fragile and conflict-affected contexts by building a stronger ecosystem of resistance against the normalisation of impunity. The programme responds to contexts where accountability is deliberately suppressed, justice institutions are captured or instrumentalised, victims are excluded from decision-making, and new technologies can deepen repression and surveillance. The programme consists of a global programme and specific in-country programmes in Chad, Syria, Tunisia and Iraq. Through these global and country-level components, it seeks to strengthen justice institutions and actors against capture and weaponisation, mobilise victims, survivors and youth as political actors, and ensure that emerging technologies are governed in rights-based, victim-centred and accountable ways. Across these objectives, Impunity Watch will combine action-oriented research, coalition-building, mobilisation and advocacy to connect grassroots demands with national, regional and international reform agendas.</narrative>
  </description>
